          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "And what should I be eating?",
          "answer": "Our library has a diet guidance summary for type 2 diabetes (National diabetes association nutrition guidance, educational summary). Some of it is useful background, but the passages I could get are incomplete, and the library does not give a specific eating plan or carbohydrate target.\n\nWhat the retrieved text says:\n- **Starch counts.** \"Sugar-free\" is not \"carbohydrate-free,\" because starch raises blood glucose about as much as sugar does.\n- **Fruit is not off-limits.** Whole fruit is part of the recommended patterns.\n- **Weight matters.** The same document says that where body weight is above the healthy range, losing weight improves glucose control. A sustained loss of about 5% gives measurable benefit, and more loss can help more.\n\nThe document also says the right carbohydrate amount is for a person's own clinician to set, which is why the system does not give a carbohydrate target. I could not retrieve the full text of that section.\n\nThe library does not cover a full meal plan for you. If you want one, ask your doctor or a registered dietitian: What carbohydrate amount suits me? Would a dietitian referral help? Should I change my diet before or after my next blood test?\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
